<div id="S5.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">High-concurrency throughput evaluation.</span> Table <a href="#S5.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ 5.2 Performance Evaluation ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ DLite: History-Free Speculative Decoding for Agentic AI" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> evaluates end-to-end throughput under concurrency from 1 to 64. <em id="S5.SS2.p4.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">DLite</em> consistently achieves higher throughput than DSpark across both model sizes and all evaluated workloads. Notably, the throughput gain remains visible even when their average acceptance lengths are close, showing that the improvement does not solely come from better draft quality. This result is consistent with the lower drafting overhead of our lightweight sequential head, which avoids the intermediate full-vocabulary projection.</p>
